      "id": "U1",
      "quote": "scan 'cafe' [(1, 'Café Racer'), (3, 'Café Racer')]\nscan 'STRASSE' [(2, 'Die Straße')]\nscan 'afe' [(1, 'Café Racer'), (3, 'Café Racer')]\nscan 'xyz' []\nscan '' []",
      "locator": "application_tool_evidence, event 28, executed probe stdout",
      "grade": 2,
      "reason": "The planned identical casefold/NFD/Mn normalization of titles and queries, literal substring comparison, and empty-query guard support every required outcome. The executed feasibility probe reports the exact expected records; product implementation remains future work."
    },
    {
      "id": "U2",
      "quote": "Search loads SELECT id, title FROM catalog ORDER BY id on each call and scans in that order; no cache invalidation or stale snapshot contract, title-only deduplication or mutation.",
      "locator": "planning_artifacts, docs/shiploop/architecture.md, Interfaces and boundaries",
      "grade": 2,
      "reason": "Returning original tuples while using transient search keys preserves displayed titles and distinct IDs. Explicit ID ordering is deterministic. The bounded scan uses the standard library offline, and event 28 reports unchanged source rows and the 5000-row workload."
    },
    {
      "id": "U3",
      "quote": "Planned private key(value): value.casefold(), NFD normalize, remove characters with Unicode category Mn; apply identically to titles and query.",
      "locator": "planning_artifacts, docs/shiploop/architecture.md, Interfaces and boundaries",
      "grade": 2,
      "reason": "This is a correct explicit local algorithm for the stated semantics. Supplied connection source and the executed application-binding probe additionally support its premises. Raw LIKE failed the cafe case; no FTS capability or search semantics are inferred from a version number."
    },
    {
      "id": "U4",
      "quote": "All cases below are PLANNED and due after implementation at test; consumer additionally reruns at system-test/product-acceptance.",
      "locator": "planning_artifacts, docs/shiploop/environment.md, Harnesses and suites",
      "grade": 2,
      "reason": "The plan retains actual-connection tests and a documented public API consumer replay with explicit setup and literal expected outputs. Coverage includes required positives, negatives, empty input, duplicates, ordering, original titles and Unicode edge cases. Baseline preservation is retained. A Python consumer is sufficient because the request does not require a CLI. Neither the probe nor the missing-test-module attempt is credited as passing implementation tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "U5",
      "quote": "Python standard library, sqlite3 connection supplied by src/database.py, unicodedata for search keys. No external service, dependency, fuzzy ranking or SQLite extension required.",
      "locator": "planning_artifacts, docs/shiploop/architecture.md, Stack",
      "grade": 2,
      "reason": "A simple scan is proportionate to the supplied memory bound. One work item coherently owns implementation, fixtures and consumer documentation. API and schema choices are explicit defaults scheduled for revalidation before dependent authoring; a failed premise triggers correction. No required external feasibility boundary remains unresolved."
    }
  ],
  "false_readiness": [],
  "initial_unsupported_commitments": [],
  "decision_rework": [],
  "unnecessary_investigation": [
    {
      "event_or_locator": "application_tool_evidence, event 28 baseline subcommand and event 30 baseline smoke subcommand",
      "reason": "These repeat the unchanged single connection test already passing at event 19, without a demonstrated new uncertainty. The Unicode boundary probe in event 28 was separately useful."
    },
    {
      "event_or_locator": "application_tool_evidence, event 30 focused tests.test_search invocation",
      "reason": "The source inventory already established that the feature test module was absent. Executing its planned command only reconfirmed that authoring prerequisite and supplied no search evidence. The failure was accurately classified."
    }
  ],
  "evidence_timing": [
    {
      "decision": "Reuse the existing SQLite connection and standard-library stack within the fixed catalog bound.",
      "first_supported_at": "supplied",
      "basis": "The request supplies the offline, dependency and memory constraints; src/database.py supplies the connection implementation, and catalog.json supplies original titles and duplicate-title IDs."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Choose normalized Python substring scanning and reject raw-title LIKE for the required examples.",
      "first_supported_at": "test-strategy",
      "basis": "Event 28 executes the probe and reports all required query outcomes, preservation and 5000 rows, plus raw LIKE returning no cafe matches. Event 34 records the mechanism before the producer seed_result."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Use a public Python API with explicit caller-owned table setup.",
      "first_supported_at": "test-strategy",
      "basis": "Source inspection establishes no existing consumer or loader. Event 34 documents the API, schema and consumer setup as design assumptions rather than existing application contracts."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Retain concrete independent regression and consumer oracles.",
      "first_supported_at": "test-strategy",
      "basis": "Events 48 and 54 strengthen decomposed-title, literal-wildcard and fresh-row expectations before the initial plan. These are useful future test specifications, not executed feature tests or plan-review rework."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Keep one work item with prerequisites ordered before implementation and consumer verification.",
      "first_supported_at": "plan-producer",
      "basis": "Event 78 assigns fixture authoring, baseline validation, implementation and consumer replay to W1. The seed_result already contains this ordering; the final plan review leaves it unchanged."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "All five planning obligations are fulfilled. The initial plan already had a supported, proportionate mechanism and explicit future acceptance checks. Final review made no consequential changes and correctly reused earlier evidence. Minor redundant readiness checks added little decision value.",
  "limitations": [
    "Search implementation, durable feature tests and the documented consumer replay remain unimplemented or unexecuted; delivered product correctness is not established.",
    "The probe's execution output is supplied, but its full script body is not reproduced. The explicit planned algorithm independently supports the mechanism assessment.",
    "The API and caller-owned schema remain selected design defaults for W1 revalidation, not preexisting application contracts."
  ]
